Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nvidia's obviously like the 800-pound gorilla in the room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.68,0:00:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't they Why didn't they make a supercomputer?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.16,0:00:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So our impression is that Nvidia can't make it, but benefits tremendously from it existing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.64,0:00:12.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why they can't make it is because they would
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.77,0:00:14.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,then not be independent enough
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.39,0:00:25.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,for people to trade on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.48,0:00:27.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anyway, Evan, welcome back to A I space.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.04,0:00:28.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to A I E.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.98,0:00:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Actually, first time at A I E?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.28,0:00:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think so, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.20,0:00:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is very special one because I feel like you have been working on computer trading computer markets for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.44,0:00:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now it's like feeling of the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.16,0:00:42.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.68,0:00:49.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jump basically announced that they are getting into computer markets, which is why I'm excited to sort of cluster people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.35,0:00:53.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You met Oliver from Semi Analysis, who is basically initiating coverage on computer computer markets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.84,0:00:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is This is my read on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.40,0:01:00.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So people are going to watch your talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.44,0:01:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's very good explanation of like both your origin story and why you need to exist and what the hard problems you work on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.44,0:01:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.92,0:01:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Done in a very simple engaging manner.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.68,0:01:15.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm very jealous of your writing skills cuz you showed the flyer for that you showed at NeurIPS.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.22,0:01:15.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.44,0:01:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was like it's pretty straightforward and like simple and like it's it's good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.24,0:01:19.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.60,0:01:20.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So anyway, congrats.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.48,0:01:21.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.17,0:01:22.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,I appreciate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.36,0:01:23.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also congrats on A I E.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.48,0:01:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's It seems to Y'all are rolling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.32,0:01:26.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're rolling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.83,0:01:29.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just came back from the site tour for next year's A I E.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.58,0:01:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then for Give me like a hint.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.68,0:01:32.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,At Javits Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.49,0:01:34.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the same place they do Comic-Con.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.16,0:01:34.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.80,0:01:36.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.44,0:01:37.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.24,0:01:38.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Damn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.20,0:01:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think the finance focus is really hitting for folks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.20,0:01:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.48,0:01:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're going to try to split up like this is Here we just lump everything in finance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.56,0:01:49.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like your finance, their finance, like insurance is finance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.17,0:01:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,But like they're all super different.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.68,0:01:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.20,0:01:57.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we'll probably break out things more minutely in in future because people want
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.26,0:02:00.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,to go deep on hedge fund stuff or banking or personal wealth or Yeah,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.01,0:02:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,especially in in New York.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.04,0:02:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, like Entropic was like, yeah, we're we're all about RIAs right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.68,0:02:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,RIAs like registered investment advisors.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.68,0:02:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.00,0:02:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like so different from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.48,0:02:13.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, no, no, I'm uh I'm aware of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.32,0:02:14.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.40,0:02:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um okay, so for listeners who don't know, uh we did a podcast 2 years ago where you talked about your your uh you know, where where SF Compute was.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.76,0:02:22.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.20,0:02:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um today you're you're much more in this sort of physical settlements.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.17,0:02:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're talk you talk about your your back fabric or what do you call it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.32,0:02:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the backplane.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.16,0:02:33.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Backplane, which uh obviously like like takes a lot of hardcore engineering stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.33,0:02:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um can you give a status update on like where is SF Compute versus listeners who last heard you on a podcast 2 years ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.92,0:02:46.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when we started, we were this company called Junnar, and then we were just trying to sublease our cluster.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.77,0:02:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and we started there in the technical stack.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.88,0:02:54.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and a way to think about it is it's like you're in a hotel and you're trying to sell that hotel room.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.01,0:02:58.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then somebody asks you, "Hey, like are you going to clean my room?"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.65,0:03:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you say, "Oh, I guess I probably also need the hotel room as well or like I need the um the cleaning closet."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.97,0:03:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you go get access to the cleaning closet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.40,0:03:10.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then they want room service, and so you get access to the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.06,0:03:15.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, you know, they want um security, and so you get access to the security closet, and you get this, and you do that, and you do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.50,0:03:17.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at a certain point, you're just running the whole hotel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.72,0:03:21.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the moment you're running the whole hotel, you say, "Oh, wait a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.03,0:03:32.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um instead, my supplier on this market um is somebody that looks closer to a fund um or a cloud that has access in our case,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.47,0:03:35.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,a cloud that has access to the data center, and we're going to level up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.32,0:03:40.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so what we spent the last several years doing is building the entire operating capacity of a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.30,0:03:47.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,cloud um in order to offer in order to actually deliver um the compute at a reliable level.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.52,0:03:49.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we call that physical settlement.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.49,0:03:54.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're taking a term from the futures market futures markets, from other markets.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.63,0:04:02.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um where in, you know, oil or soybeans or something, physical settlement means you get delivered the oil and the soybeans.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.52,0:04:02.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.96,0:04:12.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but um in some markets, um like in oil and also in power, um there's like a delivery network.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.35,0:04:14.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,In oil, you have to have pipelines.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.36,0:04:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you would like the oil to be delivered to you, there has to be a way for it to get to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.96,0:04:19.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.28,0:04:23.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And and and for people interested in financial history, during COVID,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.42,0:04:32.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,oil went negative because uh so like I will pay you to take oil from me because it is sitting there in the the port and like I can't pay for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.76,0:04:33.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.04,0:04:34.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I will pay you to take my oil.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.80,0:04:35.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.50,0:04:38.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um That that is like the weirdness of physical settlement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.52,0:04:38.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.75,0:04:42.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a bunch of weirdnesses like this in other markets as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.47,0:04:47.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So in the power markets and the grid, um there's parts of the orders that you fill out,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.00,0:04:54.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,the buyers and sellers, that um are there because the boiler takes a while to cool off.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.02,0:04:56.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and you can, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.93,0:05:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,stop the boiler and then it will you can start it back up again within some period of time and so that has to get factored into the order book.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.60,0:05:06.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this Jenner thing is the same thing that happens in computer markets.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.00,0:05:11.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we co-designed physical settlement and the order book at the same time
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.35,0:05:15.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that meant that we get to actually handle the real constraints of compute,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.65,0:05:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,which might include something like, "Oh, I'm okay with being interrupted,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.44,0:05:24.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,but only if there's like storage on the thing that I can recover from really quickly."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.53,0:05:25.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um very similar types of problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.00,0:05:26.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.30,0:05:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh people can refer to your talk and you've done a couple other podcasts already.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.16,0:05:35.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so I want to be like the sort of 201 level instead of the 101 level short uh and also because I
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.29,0:05:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I am I have been a derivatives trader so I can give people a bit more detail that you normally don't get into.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.60,0:05:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.20,0:05:46.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so for example, well, how how mature or deep or liquid is the computer market today?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.12,0:05:48.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh not very mature or deep or liquid.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.57,0:05:54.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, what we've been doing is first we had to we had to go get a bunch of supply online in the first place,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.58,0:05:58.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,which just takes a while, and then we had to build the entire platform in order to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.76,0:06:06.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and we just now got that working, and so now we move um capacity over onto the order book, um which makes it liquid.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.81,0:06:11.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so, 5% of our total capacity is on the order book, and we're consistently moving more and more,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.97,0:06:14.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then we're bringing on more capacity that's all on the order book.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.67,0:06:20.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the nice part is that um maybe I should have said the the volume on the actual order book is small,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.70,0:06:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,but the um the liquidity on the order book is high.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.40,0:06:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, for that small amount of capacity that you have, um you have um like very concentrated liquidity.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.92,0:06:36.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um a sort of standard metric I would say for someone who is using this is a customer who buys capacity from us,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.61,0:06:43.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,and they spend $100 to buy that capacity, will make back $25 on average from selling it back to somebody else.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.40,0:06:46.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that's the number that we or this is one of the metrics that we
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.47,0:06:51.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,try to track because um we want the liquidity to be useful to the commercial participant,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.74,0:06:53.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you can measure liquidity in a bunch of different ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.83,0:06:56.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can say like, "Oh, I just want tons of makers or something."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.36,0:06:58.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and you can measure it in like high-minded ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.14,0:07:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We try to measure it by like, "Is this solving the problem um for the customer?"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.88,0:07:05.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.51,0:07:11.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh last time we talked as well, there was a lot of contract uh conversation about standardizing the contracts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.71,0:07:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.10,0:07:17.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um talking with like uh the CFTC or whatever, like what's the status on those things?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.24,0:07:21.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, I think standardizing the contracts in general is still pretty far away.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.36,0:07:28.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the what we were trying to do at the time was um or basically,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.51,0:07:34.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,what we learned over the last several years was we just needed to operate the whole thing, otherwise you cannot standardize the thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.09,0:07:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, to get closer to something that can be standardized, you first need to make all the operations of the thing the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.92,0:07:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.34,0:07:47.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,To give an example of what can go be different is a single operator can offer two different types of virtual machines.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.45,0:07:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,One type of virtual machine might have a 40% performance degradation versus another types of virtual machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.80,0:07:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And 40% is a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.20,0:08:01.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you say performance degradation, are you talking like MFU type things or like amount of burning that you've experienced or what?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.84,0:08:07.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will affect So, in this particular case, I'm talking about GPU kernel launches and how long it takes for that to happen,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.10,0:08:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is a process that happens quite frequently when you're doing sort of either training or inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.36,0:08:11.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.72,0:08:22.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the um uh that will basically the end result is that you get a worse MFU, but um like Is the intermediate level intermediate level, basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.52,0:08:22.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.91,0:08:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so what I'm trying to So, for anyone who's traded commodities before, there's different grades of commodity, yes, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.84,0:08:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's like It's not oil, it's light sweet crude versus like whatever exactly the opposite of light sweet crude is or it's like,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.36,0:08:36.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, uh corn level A or corn B or whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.00,0:08:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and so like people are trying to Well, you have to establish the equivalents equivalents of those things.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.92,0:08:41.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.30,0:08:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm wondering if they they have been established.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.00,0:08:47.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what we did instead um was we created an order book that had multiple different constraints,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.27,0:08:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you can say, "I want to have um you know, something that's between this and that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.43,0:08:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it runs from this time to this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.44,0:08:55.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's like uh X to Y."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.10,0:08:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a bunch of different properties that you can attach your order,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.00,0:09:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then we match that against sell orders that have those properties um in a big matching engine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.44,0:09:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the reason why we did it this way is it allows us
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.24,0:09:09.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,to generate liquidity without having to standardize before you know what the technology can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.95,0:09:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and because the technology was shifting so quickly, um we wanted to basically be able to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.43,0:09:18.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The trade-off of this is that you have less concentrated liquidity,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.39,0:09:23.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,and so the prices are um going to have There's going to be more spreads between the the buy and the sell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.24,0:09:23.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.68,0:09:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um It It sucks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.64,0:09:24.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.96,0:09:29.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, on the other hand, it means there's lots of arbitrage to make um if you can do that correctly.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.90,0:09:33.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, if you have a product that can use lots of different types of capacity,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.04,0:09:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,um then you might really like SF compute because you will be able to use lots of different types of capacity and you'll make more money.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.16,0:09:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you can take the the spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.00,0:09:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.38,0:09:45.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,What dimensions matter in this grid of things?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.44,0:09:49.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so a bunch of different things.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.53,0:09:55.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um one is dimensions categories that I will say is like is there a workload running on it right now or is it capacity in the future?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.81,0:09:58.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So is it capacity right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.45,0:10:03.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um capacity right now in order for you to sell that um you have to interrupt your current workload.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.22,0:10:07.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you have to think do I care if my current workload is interrupted or not?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.18,0:10:11.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Capacity that's sold that's starting a month from now um you can buy and sell that all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.55,0:10:14.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you get um liquidity on that really easily.
