Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.04,0:30:48.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're we're not in the data center business, sort of.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.34,0:30:53.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, what we do work with is So, we offer supercomputing as a service.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.66,0:31:03.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and what this means is folks come to us and say, you know, I've got X, where X is I've got, you know, X megawatts here,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.71,0:31:10.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,and maybe sometimes they mean, I've got a data center um that's like I would like to turn into a GPU cluster.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.24,0:31:15.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like my options are I could sell the GPU cluster or I could sell the data center to somebody or I could become the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.76,0:31:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we go to them and say, great, um we will turn you into the cloud, we're the supercomputing part, you're the data center cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.04,0:31:24.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's partner together and then we will sell and all make money.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.74,0:31:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um sometimes it's people who have something that could turn into a data center,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.80,0:31:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,in which case we're going to basically project manage that up to the layer,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:33.76,0:31:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and then we will work with those far we'll work with those folks to turn
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.16,0:31:44.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,their powered land um or whatever they have um into a data center by working with partners,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.22,0:31:46.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and then we take over at the supercomputing part.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.87,0:31:53.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,This requires us to have some sort of data center expertise in-house, but we don't self-perform builds.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.79,0:31:55.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.32,0:32:00.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so it's somewhat modular because you have different scenarios you need to deploy under.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.32,0:32:00.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.61,0:32:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,someone once described us as like um uh like Palantir for compute um because it's like these each time
Dialogue: 0,0:32:08.64,0:32:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's this new rodeo um uh but and we like we we deeply partner with folks on both sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.04,0:32:15.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.62,0:32:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and primarily the US?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.04,0:32:20.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Primarily the US, but we operate around the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.76,0:32:21.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.03,0:32:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,At some point does SF Compute become a misnomer?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.72,0:32:28.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so, when so, we're deploying clusters all around the world, and when we do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.73,0:32:32.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're working with people who themselves are trying to be clouds all around the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.54,0:32:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um they look like sovereign compute players.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.56,0:32:38.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and our pitch to sovereign compute is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.11,0:32:43.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's help you set up a cloud in your own country and we will bring the San Francisco off-take.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.34,0:32:45.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll bring the San Francisco expertise.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.35,0:32:47.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll set up the clusters.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.20,0:32:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's our whole business.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.08,0:32:48.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.68,0:32:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to make it financeable.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.88,0:32:53.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,who are your main your biggest announced partners that you can name?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.24,0:32:56.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Nobody I can name basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.99,0:33:02.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We will have some announcements in a week or two that we expect to come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.92,0:33:03.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.56,0:33:05.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,All things sort of uh Sure, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.84,0:33:06.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.47,0:33:06.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.81,0:33:07.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,No,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.04,0:33:13.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean I I think this is really interesting for every country to like who's who's like investing in sovereign AI to figure this
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.92,0:33:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,out and it's interesting that like SF is is still sort of like that brand name and that that is that is very marketable.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.88,0:33:25.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think one of the interesting things is just thinking through this market.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.12,0:33:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.32,0:33:29.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nvidia is obviously like the 800-lb gorilla in the room.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.96,0:33:32.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't they Why didn't they make SF Compute?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.36,0:33:38.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And again like I I you know, the answer's going to be market manipulation but like let's just really get into the incentives of the multiple players.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.52,0:33:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so our impression is that Nvidia can't make it but benefits tremendously from it existing.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.19,0:33:49.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why they can't make it is because they would then not be independent enough for people to trade on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.57,0:33:55.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you don't trade on it, then you don't have enough liquidity for lenders to finance against the forwards market.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.66,0:34:00.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is also why Crusoe and Coreweave and Lambda why the hyperscalers can't make it,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.60,0:34:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,why Base10 and Fireworks and Modal can't make it cuz they have too much demand on that side.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.04,0:34:12.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this is the thing that benefits the entire industry because it makes the financing costs go down.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.17,0:34:19.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,But nobody can make it unless they give up the ability to do all the big inference money and all the big cloud deals.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.76,0:34:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to kill your business in order to make this.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:21.88,0:34:22.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.11,0:34:23.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why nobody does it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.37,0:34:25.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like structurally they're not set up to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.69,0:34:30.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're you're make you're basically reducing friction and that's all your revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.48,0:34:33.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've announced some benchmark uh, some milestones.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.40,0:34:35.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Actually, I forgot to s- say that up front.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:35.71,0:34:39.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, can you repeat what they are and uh, you know, just take a victory lap a little bit?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.04,0:34:44.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, we closed several hundred million dollars of volume.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.26,0:34:48.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, we have a significant number of new clusters on the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.30,0:34:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and then the things that I think I'm most excited about um, is we've um,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.52,0:35:02.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,shipped a whole bunch of new features um, that make SF Compute very viable for platform as a service companies.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.53,0:35:10.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, an example is um, we allow customers to subdivide their InfiniBand fabric um, without having to ask us.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.47,0:35:14.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, many clouds when you go to buy them, they will give you one InfiniBand fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.53,0:35:23.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and then if you want to re redraw the lines of that InfiniBand fabric, uh, you need to contact them and they will then do something for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.70,0:35:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, we now can do that on the fly for customers um, which I think is really great um, because it interfaces with the market really well um,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.06,0:35:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,where you want to be able to redraw things in order to scale up and down your clusters.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.36,0:35:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, would you describe this as like you're virtualizing the data center and making it programmable?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.44,0:35:41.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we're virtualizing data center and making it programmable.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.63,0:35:49.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, all the stuff that you would have gotten if you had owned the hardware, we're trying to virtualize that um, which I think is um, exciting to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.36,0:35:53.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's funny like the last time this happened was like the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.08,0:35:54.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.22,0:35:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, which is which is really cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.20,0:36:02.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, and then uh, uh, finally I you know, I think uh, what is your call to action for for people um, you know, is it is it engineers?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.90,0:36:04.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it like give me your supply?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.20,0:36:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.28,0:36:08.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, if you would like to own a GPU cluster and you want the residual value from it,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.87,0:36:13.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,you want to have it for your portfolio, um, we would love to work with you in order to build that GPU cluster.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.01,0:36:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We will take over and we will uh, do the supercomputing portions of that and ensure the things go right.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.32,0:36:20.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We own the SLA.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.14,0:36:23.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then if it turns out that that was a bad idea, that you need out of that cluster,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.68,0:36:27.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can immediately sell that cluster to with else so it doesn't hit your balance sheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.68,0:36:28.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very simple pitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.40,0:36:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, thank you so much for your time.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.80,0:36:33.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're You're doing a great service to the industry and I just am happy to be your friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.68,0:36:35.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I appreciate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.32,0:36:36.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.60,0:36:37.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's it.
